# - In this platform, they can go to the HRMS work instead of going to other tools.
# - In this platform, they can do the PM work instead of going to Linear.
# - In this platform, they can go for the CRM instead of going to other tools.
# So far, inventory,inbox, calendar, notifications, everything in one platform. That's what I want to build.
# - Who actually opens the streamlinesos account? They become the organization owner, and who are all invited? They have attached the member role or the admin role at the org level based on the role they have invited.
# - Members and admins can have their own organization and they are attached with multiple organizations.
# - The admin is equivalent to the owner except changing the owner role, and the members have access to only two screens:
# - for org admin and org owner access to all the modules and settings, and for the members, they have access to only two screens: Home and Knowledge Base.
# - Knowledge Base, where they can write documents, files, and all knowledge base content either org level or else at that user level
# - If they are invited to other modules, they can have access to those modules based on the permission given by the owner or admin of that module based on that he has a access to buttons and those pages and they only visiable else they will not be visible.
# - At each module level, there is an owner, member, and admin. For example, in a company, there is a head, so HR is responsible for the HR module. Under HR, there are multiple people who are either HR module admins or HR module members. same goes for the payroll module, same goes for the build module, and same goes for the inventory module. 
# - The owner of the module can create a permission and attach it to a specific person so that person has access to those screens with those actions in that screen he had access they will be visible. If he doesn't have access to the button, then he will not be able to see that button.
# now your task is to check the existing repo, and you have to find the best architecture which is suitable. Right now, I feel the architecture is not correct. If it is correct, then leave it as it is. If it is not correct/better architecture, then you have to go ahead and develop the best architecture for it.right now you should only focus and task scope is about proper RBAC at the module level and at the org level. proper billing, proper chat, calendar, notifications, inbox, knowledgebase, wiki, chatbot, It should scale for millions of users, and it should be easy to maintain and extend in the future. You have to provide me with a detailed architecture plan, including the following:
# 1. **Overall System Architecture**: Describe the high-level architecture of the platform, including the main components, their interactions, and how they fit together to achieve the platform's goals. Include diagrams if necessary.
